# Copy to `.buckconfig.local` (gitignored) and fill in your remote-execution
# service to build there instead of on your machine. Without this file every
# action runs locally; with `[komira_re]
  # The exact REAPI platform property set every Linux x86_64 action carries,
  # as comma-separated key=value pairs. Your service chooses the worker for
  # each action; the build states nothing about worker classes. Workers
  # match a set exactly: a key the workers do not advertise leaves actions
  # queued until the scheduler gives up. See tools/build/platforms/README.md.
  linux_properties = pool=default
  # Optional: macOS arm64 workers, for `--target-platforms
  # komira//tools/build/platforms:darwin-arm64`: their exact property set
  # (different from the linux one), and the host identity each prints for
  # `sh tools/build/mojo/darwin/host_identity.sh`, separated by spaces. See
  # tools/build/toolchains/README.md, "macOS".
  # darwin_properties = pool=macos
  # darwin_macos_hosts = 26.5-0123456789abcdef 26.5-fedcba9876543210
